# Website backend enum label mirror

Authority: `backend/src/resources/trans/ar/general.ts` and `backend/src/resources/trans/en/general.ts` under `enums.*`.

## Rule

When website UI shows a **backend enum value** as a human label (chips, filters, badges, status lines), the Arabic and English strings MUST match that enum’s `label` in backend `general.ts` for the same locale.

Shipped examples that must stay aligned:

| Backend enum | Value | ar `label` | en `label` |
|---|---|---|---|
| `meetingStatus` | `DRAFT` | مسودة | Draft |
| `meetingStatus` | `WAITING_TO_START` | بانتظار البدء | Waiting to start |
| `meetingStatus` | `STARTED` | بدأ | Started |
| `meetingStatus` | `COMPLETED` | مكتمل | Completed |
| `meetingStatus` | `CANCELED` | ملغى | Canceled |
| `meetingType` | `PERIODIC` | دوري | Periodic |
| `meetingType` | `EMERGENCY` | طارئ | Emergency |
| `meetingParticipantType` | `CHAIRPERSON` / `MEMBER` / `VIEWER` | رئيس الاجتماع / عضو / مشاهد | Chairperson / Member / Viewer |

Website keys that restate these values (e.g. `meetingLayout.init.statusStarted`, `pages.customer.meetings.statusStarted`, home STARTED badges) are **mirrors**, not a second vocabulary.

## Forbidden

- Invented synonyms for the same enum value (e.g. «جارٍ» / «جاري» / “In progress” / “Live” for `STARTED`).
- Changing only the website string when the backend label is the product authority — update backend `general.ts` first (both ar + en), then mirror into website.
- Treating loading/connecting UX copy (“جاري التحميل…”) as a `meetingStatus` label — those are unrelated.

